    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1166">

                <pb facs="1362" n="1164" sameAs="frus:frus1945Berlinv02/pg1164"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 Control (Italy)/7–2345</note>
                <head>No. 1166<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">The Assistant Secretary of State</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Dunn</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of the Soviet Delegation</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Novikov</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Berlin</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1945-07-27">July 27, 1945</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Mr. Novikov</hi>: I refer to your note of July
                    23, 1945<anchor n="1" xml:id="d1166-f1"/> with which you enclosed an <hi
                        rendition="#italic">aide-mémoire</hi> in regard to the British camp for
                    Soviet citizens in the region of Cesenatico (Italy).</p>
                <p>Since this is entirely a British matter I assume that you will approach the
                    British separately and that your <hi rendition="#italic">aide-mémoire</hi> was
                    transmitted for information purposes only.</p>
                <p>Sincerely yours,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">James Clement
                    Dunn</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
